<title>UK: Kellogg sets $500 million four-year bond, +7 bp.</title>
<headline>Kellogg sets $500 million four-year bond, +7 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Lehman Brothers and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KELLOGG CO</p>
<p> AMT    $500 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    06.AUG.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE   L05.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+7 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>	    L LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.40	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND THREE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	NO 144A</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
